==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:EU_location_EST.png|thumb|200 px|Location of Estonia]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|Esthonia||dated}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ML.|Estonia}}. Other early Latin forms were {{m|la|Estia}} and {{m|la|Hestia}}, possibly derived from the tribal name {{m|la|Aestiī}} described by the [[Roman]] historian [[w:Tacitus|Tacitus]] in his Germania (ca. 98 AD). Displaced {{cog|enm|Ēstland}}, from {{cog|ang|Ēstland}}. Compare also {{cog|non|Æistland}}, {{cog|is|Eistland}}, {{cog|de|Estland||Estonia}}.

===Pronunciation===
